    "narrative": "For LawDog today, **Lawrence Butler** (72.82) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) represent our most potent offensive levers. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a dynamic platoon advantage against Rocker, vaulting his efficiency score well into the \"Strong\" category. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** thrives against Bassitt, with his projected output buoyed by a +19% SP skill adjustment and a favorable 2-hole spot in the order. Both players are prime candidates for high-volume production in the R, HR, and RBI categories, effectively insulating our daily efficiency floor.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed our lineup cutoff with a score of 39.41. While his matchup against Jobe offered a positive park factor, the significant negative adjustment for Jobe\u2019s SP skill suppressed his ceiling just enough to keep him on the bench behind **JJ Bleday** and **Jung Hoo Lee**. Elsewhere, we are monitoring **Gleyber Torres** (59.94) closely; despite a tough matchup against Newcomb, his leadoff spot and L/L platoon adjustment keep him just shy of the \"Strong\" threshold. We remain cautious regarding **Jung Hoo Lee** (45.16) and **JJ Bleday** (48.36), as both occupy the lower end of our starting efficiency range, making them primary candidates for mid-game swaps should more favorable pinch-hit options emerge.\n\nRisk assessment remains stable across the board, though we must navigate the 53% SB suppression adjustment currently tempering the output for **Masyn Winn**. While **Masyn Winn** is usually a cornerstone for our scarce SB category, facing Holmes necessitates a disciplined approach. We are effectively managing our game caps by keeping **Gavin Sheets** sidelined; his sub-40 score against a challenging arm like Williams makes him an easy scratch. Ensure all attention is on the final confirmation of the batting orders for **Cal Raleigh** and **Brendan Donovan** to ensure their positional adjustments hold firm before the first pitch.",
